Implement a professional ticket panel with an embed, top banner, bottom banner, and a select menu.

Provide five configurable ticket categories:

1. General Support
2. High Rank Support
3. Report a Member
4. Ban Appeal
5. Recruitment Support

Allow each category to configure:
- Display name and emoji.
- Description.
- Support role IDs to ping.
- Staff access role IDs.
- Category/channel ID for ticket creation.
- Ticket opening message.
- Top banner URL.
- Bottom banner URL.
- Transcript settings.
- DM settings.
- Optional ticket questions.

The ticket selection panel should be a polished rich embed with a select menu.

When a user selects a category:
1. Validate the selection.
2. Prevent duplicate open tickets when configured.
3. Generate a unique ticket number.
4. Create a ticket channel with a readable name such as `high-rank-support-5398`.
5. Apply correct private channel permissions.
6. Grant access to the ticket opener and the configured support roles.
7. Ping only the configured support roles for that ticket type.
8. Send the ticket opening embed with the top banner, instructions, and buttons.
9. Include Claim, Close, Add Member, Remove Member, and Transcript actions as appropriate.
10. Record the ticket in SQLite.
11. Log the creation event.
12. Send a success response with a real link to the ticket channel.

The success message should resemble:

“Successfully created your ticket — [Open Ticket]”

Use a real Discord channel link generated from the channel ID. Never hardcode a fake URL.

## Ticket naming and numbering
- Use a persistent database counter or unique ticket ID.
- Do not reuse ticket numbers after a restart.
- Support concurrent ticket creation without duplicate numbers.
- Store ticket opener, type, channel ID, ticket number, handler, creation time, and closure details.

## Claiming
- Allow only configured support roles to claim tickets.
- Store the claimed-by user ID.
- Prevent unauthorized claim/unclaim actions.
- Log claims and releases.

## Closing
When a ticket closes:
- Ask for an optional closure reason.
- Record the closer and handler separately.
- Record the opened and closed timestamps.
- Calculate duration correctly.
- Capture the conversation before deleting the channel.
- Generate the transcript and save its URL.
- Send the user a DM with a professional closure embed.
- Send a copy or link to the configured audit channel.
- Delete or archive the channel according to configuration.
- Handle DM failures without undoing the closure.
- Never claim a transcript was uploaded unless the upload actually succeeded.

Example DM:

Ticket #5398 — High Rank Support

Your High Rank Support ticket has been closed.

Handled By: @Handler
Closed By: @Closer

Opened: October 28, 2026 at 3:08 PM
Closed: [actual closure time]
Duration: 11m
Messages Sent: 6 messages

[View Online Transcript]

Use real users, timestamps, durations, and message counts from stored data. Do not hardcode example names or dates.

## Ticket transcript requirements
- Support HTML transcripts with readable message formatting.
- Include usernames, display names, message timestamps, edited markers, and attachment links.
- Escape HTML to prevent injection.
- Preserve messages in chronological order.
- Paginate/fetch message history safely.
- Include ticket metadata and closure information.
- Handle deleted users, deleted attachments, embeds, and missing content gracefully.
- Restrict access to private transcripts.
- Store the transcript URL and generation status in SQLite.

Integrate with Cookie API at https://www.cookie-api.com/ when its documented API supports the required upload operation.

Do not invent Cookie API endpoints, authentication headers, or request bodies. Read the official API documentation and implement its actual interface. Put the API key in `COOKIE_API_KEY`. If the API cannot be accessed or its documentation is insufficient, implement a local HTML transcript generator and a configurable alternative upload provider. Clearly explain the fallback.

An online transcript button must point to the real URL returned by the successful upload. Do not generate fake transcript links.

